Replay of Chloe's real-ISO 095-03 Check failure (Devuan mirror ftp.fau.de unreachable).

update.stderr and the Err:/continuation lines in update-*.stdout are transcribed
verbatim from /workspace/lcos-iso-qa/results/095-03/bios-inst-u1c-after-check-maximized.png
(and bios-inst-u1c-after-check.png). The u1-*.txt logs from that run record the
marker and package state but not the apt-get update output or its exit code.

update-partial.stdout adds Hit: lines for the two sources on the ISO that were
still reachable (config/includes.chroot/etc/apt/sources.list.d/lcos-overlay.list
and config/archives/brave.list.chroot in lcos-live 0.9.5). With them the real
helper reports STATUS up-to-date plus WARN lines that start with
"W: Failed to fetch", which is the text Chloe saw. update-total.stdout has no
Hit: line (every source down) and gives STATUS error.

apt-get update normally exits 0 when only index fetches fail; the tests replay
both exit 0 and exit 100.
